          "filename": "Children's flower fete in park adjoining Recreation Institute at Letchworth Park, Hertfordshire, England(GN01775A).jpg",
          "caption": "Letchworth Garden City Recreation Institute  exterior view,  Hertfordshire, England See also GN01775, 1786A, 1787\nLetchworth Garden City, commonly known as Letchworth,  in Hertfordshire, England. 1916.  It is a former civil parish. See also GN01775A, 1786, 1787\n\nBritain's first planned “garden city,” much copied elsewhere,  was founded in 1903 by Sir Ebenezer Howard, founder of the new town movement. The commercial centre and the residential and industrial areas are carefully separated. Industries include engineering, printing and publishing, and light manufactures. Wikipedia",
